{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle","id":1493251,"title":"Mieyerditch: What if the kindred did want to treat the kine like cattle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-18T10:48:33-07:00","id":1493251,"title":"Mieyerditch: What if the kindred did want to treat the kine like cattle?","content":"In all likelihood if the Masquerade was ever truly broken I think the vampires would immediately take charge of the media narrative and control the situation: while there would be a few shakeups the status quo wouldn't change much and the average person, much less anyone with actual power, would do nothing to confront the bloodsuckers. Vampires would hide the extent of their wrongdoings and present themselves as a fearful and wrongly persecuted minority. For everyone with power, this is a status quo they want to keep. For the usual firebrands, they will remain quiet in the face of an actual threat. For the average person, it's not going to affect your day job and not worth sticking your neck out for. Most people tend to be more reasonable than given credit for. <br /> <br /> That said. <br /> What if someone was crazy enough to try open rule of mortals and large-scale containment? Maybe they've got delusions of grandeur, an axe to grind, or just got really bored over the centuries. Maybe there was a kindred-kine war that got ugly. Or maybe to combat the continuing rise of progressive and egalitarian thought which would create hellish conditions for vampires, vampires have resorted to draconian control to stop their extinction. There's a few good depictions in media like Mieyerditch in runescape, Carmilla's plan in the Castlevania series, I'm sure I've seen it somewhere else less well done. I think there are a few more fantastical post-apocalyptic fictions where vampires benefit IE the smoke blocks the sun all the time. But I'm unsure if turning much of the world to a wasteland would be good for vampires or not. I can think of why it might be useful for coercing the population to stay in their pens, but VTM vampires don't benefit from the creepy atmosphere so many other vampires do/food issues. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think it'd be very doable. With Ghouling, Dominate, a clear hierarchy where collaborators benefit, modern and near-future technology (InB4 the real world's fully automated police state) plus a little bit of Vicissitude, necromancy and thaumaturgy could help. Without the concerns for the masquerade and greater populace control the ratio of vampires to people could probably increase by tens of folds. I'd assume vampires would leave behind humanity and switch to something like honourable accord. Vampires have huge numerical and logistical advantages over garou and mages so I'd also assume they'd win any war <br /> <i>Extra crazy: The Red Talons and other more extreme garou are actually happy with the arrangement. Humans controlled=less despoiled nature= Happy werewolves.</i> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I was curious, how do people think this process would happen? I had ideas for a character that wanted to push the idea. But I'm interested in what everyone else thinks. Leaders being what they are, I think they'd sell us into it: better a good position in hell than a bad one in heaven / Better bled than red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T11:04:12-07:00","id":1493253,"title":"","content":"If I were a vampire sect who wanted to openly rule, I would gain subtle control over the dominant country's politicians. Through them I would instigate continual wars to drain those countries' resources, stir up ethnic conflict within those nations through mass immigration, create an economic system whereby a cashless society would be happily accepted by the population, mass media is controlled by my sycophants, and anyone who attempts to fight me gets unpersoned, and their assets are frozen or confiscated. Have the media glorify being a vampire, make everyone want to be one, Hell, start a religion or three. <br /> <br /> At that point, I would create political opposition movements based on just enough truth to sneak the large lies by, monitor them, and unperson anyone whose power level gets too high. <br /> <br /> Any time vampires are criticized, they deflect and bring up the Inquisition, and how so many ancient vampires were killed. <br /> <br /> Simple as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T11:54:10-07:00","id":1493258,"title":"","content":"Vampires should really do this underground. There should have long since been underground cities full of vampires and humans raised from birth to worship them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:05:13-07:00","id":1493260,"title":"","content":"I'd be careful with this idea as it strays dangerously close to the sort of stuff that went on during WWII. Treating people like cattle is a short steep path to hell.<br /> <br /> Also, in game terms, it's a rapid loss of humanity for all involved, which means that the beast soon takes over and then you've got a whole load of feral vampires ripe for the staking. Not a good plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:09:50-07:00","id":1493261,"title":"","content":"There are several aspects to this that hinge on certain tropes being used, but perhaps more importantly certain realities being ignored.<br /> <br /> First is that Kindred have a natural control over how often they create more kindred, which means you can have very specific number ratios when it comes to how many kine-cattle each kindred needs to own. This is turn means that as long as you have isolation from the rest of the world, a vampire rancher is more or less self-sufficient.<br /> <br /> Second is that since kindred are immortal, they can create really long-term plans, like keeping and breeding your own mortal society with no training or knowledge except what you give them. Furthermore, unlike slave groups from IRL history, a little Dominate ensures allows you to find out who is loyal and who is secretly gaining knowledge, no capoeira for your food supply. This means the cattle will have a completely different culture, different language, and values than the normal mortals. This also means that if the mortals can not break the system, then all the vampire has to do is suppress knowledge of a different way of life and wait for everyone to die from old age.<br /> <br /> Third is that a vampire wants human blood, and unless you are a Ventrue or perhaps a Salubri, you don't need a fully functional human to get it. A small easily maintained group of lobotomized humans or mortals put into medically induced comas can take care of your needs. Yes they will die eventually from lack of movement, but they are replaceable.<br /> <br /> There are many ways to have the mortals be cattle, but when you think about it, open rulership doesn't really give substantial benefits, just ego boosts. It is far better to have a sealed off underground city like in Seraph of the End, or disabled humans like in Daybreakers acting as blood farms.<br /> <br /> If you must have an open rule system, then I would suggest invoking the mentality of Carl Schmitt and have the reveal of vampires be carefully staged. Have an artificial enemy attack humanity, then once humanity is on the brink, the Vampires come out of hiding and save the day.... or night in this case. Thus as humanities saviors, they form symbiotic communities.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce flesh crafted monsters can be used to create the fake enemy, but given that they are just at best ghouls, means that mortal weaponry is going to be too functional against them. The few necromancer clans/bloodlines could probably do better mass summoning violent wraiths or just importing Specters to rampage around. Warding magic would by default make the vampire owned lands the only safe areas, thus automatic rulership. The key thing is that whatever you use as the artificial enemy, you need to make sure they can't communicate and reveal the con.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:15:37-07:00","id":1493263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493260#post1493260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be careful with this idea as it strays dangerously close to the sort of stuff that went on during WWII. Treating people like cattle is a short steep path to hell.<br /> <br /> Also, in game terms, it's a rapid loss of humanity for all involved, which means that the beast soon takes over and then you've got a whole load of feral vampires ripe for the staking. Not a good plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this amusing since humanity regularly treats certain classes of people like cattle, one could argue it is a very human thing to do.<br /> <br /> But discussions on the human condition aside, on a mechanics level this would just mean that the Path of Humanity becomes less common amongst the kindred in that society. Sure the average Humanity based vampire will be running around with a rating of 5 or 6, but they won't be feral beasts either. Unless you are the type to suggest that treating cattle like cattle somehow equals sociopathy rather than just being a responsible and caring farmer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:18:59-07:00","id":1493264,"title":"","content":"I think they simply would kick back humanity in to the stone age and would keep them there this time<br /> Vampires have 0 use of technology and as former humans usually terrified of the new things and change<br /> Not to mention, when you have magic and powers? Technology is more of a nuisance<br /> The only thing Humanity have is Technology beyond the vampires understanding (numerical advantage is nothing when Dominate, Presence or magic is at your fingertip) and most of the Sires embrace out of desperation to keep in touch with the modern times.<br /> And they don't even have to be Elders, in the past two decades Technology advanced considerably and even Generation Z (not to mention Millenials or Generation X or the Silent Generation) have problems to embrace and understand what is the norm for Generation Alpha<br /> And they totally could do it<br /> While Technology advanced and Humanity as a Race became smarter, on the individual level, collectively beacame dumber and dependent of technology.<br /> We have started building a more stupidity-inducing environment.Tech obsession might be to blame, but as the decline started in the 1970s, well before everyone spent their days staring at screens, that can't be the whole story. Other proposed explanations are unhealthy modern diets, increasingly trashy media, or a decline in the quality of schooling or the prevalence of reading.<br /> We became so dependent of the technology, without it, we have serious problems. We are not learning anymore, we are just know where to look it up on the net.<br /> Heck, nowdays it is common for children to not really know how what handwriting/cursive is and how to do it or read it, because they learned it on a tablet or computer...<br /> The Mad Max-style post-apoclyptic world is just around the corner... and it would only took a few short year to go from today to there or deeper, back to the stone age<br /> Take away the energy-grid and the world basically crumble, round up the (very very very) few who knows the secret of smithing and such, and let the Human nature take control eg. the herd menality kicks in; give them a (Blood)god/Protector/Tyrant to follow, devide the world in to domains, rulled by ancient monsters... and before you know it, they will forget modern world even existed within a decade!<br /> (The Garou probably woud even help!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:46:33-07:00","id":1493268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493258#post1493258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires should really do this underground. There should have long since been underground cities full of vampires and humans raised from birth to worship them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've thought about it. I think you could easily pull some vault-tech style shenanigans. For small scale experiments it will work well but I think you'd be very limited in scale and wouldn't have enough of a city to really have a full political hellscape with vampires working in tandem to keep things nightmarish. You might as well just have a commune. With today's depopulation there's plenty of ghost towns to take advantage of.<br /> <br /> underground building is difficult even when you have the resources: it grabs attention. An island or something in the midst of nowhere would be easier for the one-city job. But, if we ever went -vampire overlords are the new norm- we're almost certainly going to build above ground. It's cheaper and easier. If you're afraid of the sun you can just mandate high walls, no windows and plenty of shelter over important streets. Lots of big indoor complexes too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493260#post1493260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be careful with this idea...</div> </div> </div> </div>At no point did I think a character planning this would be heroic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-18-2022, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T13:51:22-07:00","id":1493279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493264#post1493264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they simply would kick back humanity in to the stone age and would keep them there this time<br /> Vampires have 0 use of technology and as former humans usually terrified of the new things and change<br /> Not to mention, when you have magic and powers? Technology is more of a nuisance</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern farming, construction techniques, sewerage, lights... Anything that allows for bigger cities is good for vampires. Designer drugs are probably fun too.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing Humanity have is Technology beyond the vampires understanding (numerical advantage is nothing when Dominate, Presence or magic is at your fingertip) and most of the Sires embrace out of desperation to keep in touch with the modern times. </div> </div> </div>While I doubt vampires are embracing microchip engineers I really don't think modern tech is &quot;beyond understanding&quot; for a population who exhibit none of the mortal detriments of aging beyond 40.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And they don't even have to be Elders, in the past two decades Technology advanced considerably and even Generation Z (not to mention Millenials or Generation X or the Silent Generation) have problems to embrace and understand what is the norm for Generation Alpha </div> </div> </div>I don't understand why Baby Shark is so in vogue with the little ones and I've been resistant towards virtual reality, but I have my doubts that Gen A will be difficult.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have started building a more stupidity-inducing environment. </div> </div> </div> what?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tech obsession might be to blame, but as the decline started in the 1970s, well before everyone spent their days staring at screens, that can't be the whole story. </div> </div> </div> I blame Thatcher and Reagan. Oh, they're 80's. NVM.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other proposed explanations are unhealthy modern diets, increasingly trashy media, or a decline in the quality of schooling or the prevalence of reading. </div> </div> </div>Diets? Maybe. Media? People forget what sucked 30 years ago to focus on the greats while hyper-focusing on what sucks today.. People remember Jaws but forget Jaws II and III. It's difficult to measure the rate of schooling but the trend is an upwards one. Kids read now more than they ever did before.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We became so dependent of the technology, without it, we have serious problems. We are not learning anymore, we are just know where to look it up on the net. </div> </div> </div>Over the past two weeks I gained expert knowledge on strength and hypertrophy training because it seemed interesting and there are several really well researched youtubers citing sources and providing easily digestible information. Before that I was going insane learning about snakes. (just don't go near them) If anything the current kids are statistically speaking some of the most well-educated kids there are and the next generation will surpass them. Meanwhile the grandparents of today are oh-so happy to believe in myths that were vigorously debunked decades ago. While I lament not having the skills of our hunter-gatherer ancestors, it's rare to find boomers so well-read or endowed with practical knowledge that eludes kids today, other than maybe car or home repair, since us youth often lack those things.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heck, nowdays it is common for children to not really know how what handwriting/cursive is and how to do it or read it, because they learned it on a tablet or computer... </div> </div> </div>While we're at it. We should lament that nobody knows the art of tapestry anymore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (The Garou probably woud even help!) </div> </div> </div> you're talking very Wyrmy here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Long story short I think Vampires will of course use tech to keep the kids in the cages. It's just to convenient. Automatic locks, cameras, electricity, industry, spying on the populace through the way they use their mobile phones... it's too good of a tool not to use it. Now, limiting how tech is used in a cult? Decent idea. But vampires benefit from most human inovations as much as humans do. The only tech disadvantageous to vampires are weapons and thermals and perhaps the social change caused by automation. Some things have problems but they come with solutions, like how you can more easily get footage of masquerade breaches but on the otherhand people are used to trickery and special effects and it's easy to say something's fake. Everything else makes unlife better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T16:50:38-07:00","id":1493295,"title":"","content":"If someone went crazy enough to try world domination and you run it with reasonable psychological and social dynamics, they would just fail. Small scale the goal is doable, large scale it is doomed.<br /> <br /> First, the notion that all vampires will just collectively go in line with this is stupid. They're still people, some will just reject such a plan on principle, many will reject it for various personal reasons, and any vampire agreeable to the idea is likely to sabotage you sooner or later for personal gain, or at least sabotage one another.<br /> <br /> Large scale wars aren't the only concern, that's not how this works. While vampires may continually outpace their destruction, this is not about other supernaturals or mortals eliminating vampires altogether, it is about denying their plans. This goal has the disadvantage of depending too much on the rigidity of such society, with no leeway for failure. Real life dictatorships have far more power than their subjects and still need to keep a police state, deal with frequent leaks of undesirable news, and constantly &quot;release pressure&quot; through the people that simply get out. The logistics of such a world is more hellish than anything the vampires can do to the people.<br /> <br /> Even a war against the Kine is a losing prospect. They're not just far more numerous, they are your food. How do you win a war against your food? If you keep them weak, they lose value, if they die they lose value, if they can't reproduce enough they lose value, everything they produce benefits you someway while making them miserable literally affects your food. Ever heard about scorched-earth strategy? The problem isn't their numbers alone, but how well mortals can resource to this.<br /> <br /> Not to talk about technology. Supernaturals have a lot of advantage as long as they don't escalate things enough. What can a Methuselah do in a nuked city? I mean, besides starving into torpor of they survive. Modern technology greatly equalize things in a large scale, far more than it does in a personal scale. And again, wiping out your food isn't exactly a victory.<br /> <br /> People are varied. As much as you can control them through fear, you can't really eliminate variation. Societies are built around control, but they always have some form of space for this variation and to deal with those who won't bend. The more rigid, the more resources you have to spend in managing this. Such a large scale domination would require massive resources and constant surveillance just to keep the status quo, if it is ever achieved to begin with, and too much to lose at any rebellion event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T19:52:18-07:00","id":1493300,"title":"","content":"To be fair there is a difference between getting rid of technology and keeping it a mysterious art of the vampires. Castlevania, Vampire Hunter D, and Trinity Blood all messed around with the notion of Vampires being the hidden keepers of lost archeo-tech.<br /> <br /> I could easily see the vampire lords living in technologically advanced fortresses, while the mortals live simplistic agrarian lives on the surface. The tricky part is do you create a privileged class of mortals who are more educated to handle thing beyond just having knowledgeable ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T22:37:58-07:00","id":1493304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493295#post1493295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone went crazy enough to try world domination and you run it with reasonable psychological and social dynamics, they would just fail. Small scale the goal is doable, large scale it is doomed.<br /> <br /> First, the notion that all vampires will just collectively go in line with this is stupid. They're still people, some will just reject such a plan on principle, many will reject it for various personal reasons, and any vampire agreeable to the idea is likely to sabotage you sooner or later for personal gain, or at least sabotage one another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that. Let's imagine a scenario where the world trends towards idealistic socialism, automation begins helping the people, the gap between rich and poor becomes positively swedish, corruption becomes harder to pull off because everyone finds prestige more important than extra money. Crime becomes the domain of crazy people since there's no financial incentive or societal presure to encourage it. The right-wing reactionary groups the vampires have been backing fall to the wayside. <br /> <br /> This is hell conditions for vampires. Vampires thrive from huge gaps between rich and poor: the rich offer entertainment and shelter while the poor offer food and easy outlets. They like that they can just throw money around and have people do their bidding. They like that the system is arranged in their favour. It's the difference between a jungle and a desert. Some vampires might resist reactionary fascism, and they might make interesting characters in the story, but if it's fascism with you as a ruler or starving in the desert as your own life becomes measurably harder to maintain, vampires tend to be selfish enough to pick whatever's best for them at the expense of others, that's literally how they survive on a night-to-night basis after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T22:45:12-07:00","id":1493306,"title":"","content":"One method to do it peaceably is move towards establishing a police state. Slowly crush civil liberties in the name of fighting terrorism. With drones and the like you can minimize how many police you actually need and simplify things. When the poor can do nothing, the rich are in your bed, the media is telling people what you want them to hear, and large numbers of people are in prisons without any hope of release, you can indulge in <s>billionaire</s> vampiric overlord fantasies (At least concerning the prisons. Most of the world might be &quot;normal&quot; enough for humane vampires)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 09-19-2022, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T00:26:42-07:00","id":1493309,"title":"","content":"Reading through this reminded me of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anno_Dracula\" target=\"_blank\">Anno Dracula</a> by Kim Newmann. It's victorian era, but same deal. Vlad kills Helsing and presses Victoria into marriage, subsequently turning the UK into a police state. Vampirism becomes a commodity, first for nobility but soon spreads into the lower society.<br /> As for the bunker stuff, you can go straight to current day <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2022/sep/04/super-rich-prepper-bunkers-apocalypse-survival-richest-rushkoff\" target=\"_blank\">billionaire doomsday preppers</a>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T07:13:21-07:00","id":1493327,"title":"","content":"\u200bI think it's important to define what does 'ruling openly' actually mean when it comes to something like this. I'm sure we all have an idea that it would be vampires as autocratic tyrants that would fill all major positions of government and humans would be nothing by cattle underneath an Empire of Blood. And while I do agree that humans would have a hard time, I don't think vampires would flood the governments mostly because I don't think they would care for the mundanity of day to day governmental proceedings.<br /> <br /> To me, 'ruling openly' just means that vampires would use their money and power to get the laws and regulations they want pass and basically do whatever. I'm sure that some vampires would take positions of power (especially in a broken masquerade scenario) but, I think the vast majority would form blocs and super pacts to just fund their way into having all the power with none of the reasonability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T07:46:45-07:00","id":1493329,"title":"","content":"It's also hard to run a government when you are asleep during the day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T11:30:14-07:00","id":1493344,"title":"","content":"To add my simplefied two cents on the matter. I can't see the kindred wanting to got this route at all, why saddle yourself with the headaches of trying to run the world and not be able to truly relax for a moment? It's much easier to simply nudge society into a direction that helps you in the long run. Being so out there creates envy and plots to unseat you or your proxies and when you are immortal and time is on your side. Why bother with such mundane goals when you can spend the time refining your powers and knowledge of the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T11:50:41-07:00","id":1493347,"title":"","content":"I agree. Most kindred are just going to enjoy their 'unlives' and do ... whatever hobbies an immortal picks up to past the time. That said, I not saying they wouldn't involve themselves in the politics of whatever country they live in to make their unlives more comfortable.<br /> <br /> I can see certain laws being passed or revoked to make getting blood easier. Special programs being taught/given about the nature of kindred. Certain churches getting support while others get labeled as hate groups. Generally things that are going to make it easier to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T14:57:16-07:00","id":1493357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493329#post1493329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also hard to run a government when you are asleep during the day</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to be an impediment for most of our governments these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T21:11:33-07:00","id":1493377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493329#post1493329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also hard to run a government when you are asleep during the day</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, not really an issue. Retainers do 90% of the small work and they probably enjoy their own degree of corruption and decadance. Perhaps the retainer is seen as a Doctor Breen Collaborator type figure; the face to look to, or perhaps a crazy vampire acts as head of state despite not really doing much kinda like the royal family in a constitutional monarchy/ the head vampire is a big ideas guy that says things and watches the little people struggle to make it happen/.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T21:35:42-07:00","id":1493380,"title":"","content":"So, just like old True Blood series... But in a non silly way heh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T01:55:35-07:00","id":1493391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493300#post1493300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could easily see the vampire lords living in technologically advanced fortresses, while the mortals live simplistic agrarian lives on the surface. The tricky part is do you create a privileged class of mortals who are more educated to handle thing beyond just having knowledgeable ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is the infrastructure needed to keep those fortresses running, specially against a rival that simply decides to go &quot;screw this BS&quot; and build a mortal army to retake the world in exchange for a less dumb society,<br /> <br /> With futuristic tech we can easily picture a bunker with all the amenities we can imagine and completely self-sustaining. But with actual modern tech this simply isn't a thing. An actual modern bunker is extremely comfortable for the standards of a cave and can keep going for decades without external resources. But they still miss a lot of actual benefits if there's no technological society outside and it <b>will</b> run out eventually, and not that much time from the perspective of a vampire.<br /> <br /> Not to say that plunging humanity back to pre-industrial times, <b>if achieved</b>, which I'm skeptical of, would impact population greatly. Just the effects on food production alone would cause widespread famine. The actual amount of tech &quot;allowed&quot; would greatly impact this, but unless those vampires are omnipresent and omniscient enough to squash any development in its crib, I'd say anything beyond the 10th century is a risk of &quot;dangerous weapons&quot; being developed and hid before they can notice, maybe not even that. So we're talking a world that sustained less than 400 million souls. Could it house more under vampire rule? Maybe, but I doubt that it would be a lot more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493304#post1493304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's imagine a scenario</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an extremely contrived scenario and still a false dichotomy within it.<br /> <br /> You're trying to equate &quot;survival&quot; with &quot;following this plan and only this plan&quot;. And the character that comes up with it probably will try to pull the same argument.<br /> <br /> But the thing is, this plan needs a huge level of agreement between them and there may simply be other plans that don't have so many problems. Even if this <b>is</b>, for some weird reason, the only way to survive, it would be necessary to <i><b>convince</b></i> almost every vampire that it is the only way to survive. It is not that some will choose to starve instead of being so &quot;evil&quot;, it is that many will have their own plans on how to survive they believe hold a better outcome for themselves.<br /> <br /> I don't have much more to say for now. I think this proposal can work in a myriad unique scenarios in very different ways, but a baseline that makes sense seems hard to come by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T02:24:28-07:00","id":1493393,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=monteparnas;n1493391]<br /> The problem is the infrastructure needed to keep those fortresses running, specially against a rival that simply decides to go &quot;screw this BS&quot; and build a mortal army to retake the world in exchange for a less dumb society,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With futuristic tech we can easily picture a bunker with all the amenities we can imagine and completely self-sustaining. But with actual modern tech this simply isn't a thing. An actual modern bunker is extremely comfortable for the standards of a cave and can keep going for decades without external resources. But they still miss a lot of actual benefits if there's no technological society outside and it <b>will</b> run out eventually, and not that much time from the perspective of a vampire. </div> </div> </div>I think it's very possible for vampires<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's an extremely contrived scenario and still a false dichotomy within it. </div> </div> </div>Imagine what Automation will do to the world. There was a statistic that suggested something like 70% of canadians are projected to lose their job this decade. Simplifying a little: When farming got mechanized people moved out of the fields and into the factories. As the factories got better mechanized people moved out from the factories into the services. Now that the services are being automated, where the fuck do people go? Either people live without scarcity in a world where machines work for the collective, which would be unfortunate for the rulling class and hell for vampires, or society will be pushed towards an authoritarian hierarchy or worse, anarcho capitalism, which is essentially fuedalism but with business owners rather than warriors. either of which are excellent for the working class and provide the best possible habbitat for vampires. Now, vampires don't need to Mieyerditch with the extreme right scenario; they could do all this stuff hidden no problem. But there lies the interesting caveat: They don't need to be hidden in this scenario. The rulers have supressed the peasantry, the rulers interests align with vampiric interests.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're trying to equate &quot;survival&quot; with &quot;following this plan and only this plan&quot;. And the character that comes up with it probably will try to pull the same argument.<br /> <br /> But the thing is, this plan needs a huge level of agreement between them and there may simply be other plans that don't have so many problems. Even if this <b>is</b>, for some weird reason, the only way to survive, it would be necessary to <i><b>convince</b></i> almost every vampire that it is the only way to survive. It is not that some will choose to starve instead of being so &quot;evil&quot;, it is that many will have their own plans on how to survive they believe hold a better outcome for themselves.<br /> <br /> I don't have much more to say for now. I think this proposal can work in a myriad unique scenarios in very different ways, but a baseline that makes sense seems hard to come by. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If there's no need for a masquerade, what do you think vampires would do? If the mortals could truly do nothing against their oppressors, would it make sense to enforce the masquerade? </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T13:20:21-07:00","id":1493424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's very possible for vampires </div> </div> </div>Please elaborate, I've never seen anything suggesting vampires have secret super technology that is better then the human standards. In fact, most vampires of standing and power dislike technology and only use it begrudgingly (it is just too useful to ignore it completely and they are pragmatists) because they are ancient old fossils that resent the world changing from the way it was 'back in their day' centuries or even millennia ago. They aren't the types to pull something like Dracula did in the Castlevania netflix show and spend their unlife mastering science and putting themselves literal centuries ahead of the rest of the world's technology. The closest I can think of is the Nosferatu making a computer program whose UI is invisible without the use of auspex, which was presented as more of a 'why would mortals bother trying to make something like that' thing then a 'only the vampires could have managed this with their super vampire science' thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T14:06:58-07:00","id":1493430,"title":"","content":"Ah yes I somehow forgot to conclude that tangent. <br /> <br /> A herd bunker doesn't need to be independent? Getting supplies from outside is easy? <br /> It's entirely possible for vampires to keep their herd in a secure place like an underground bunker or prison and have them fed and supplied by farms and other stuff outside the facility. Today's farming technology is pretty great so vampires will have an easy time using a few easily controlled farmers to provide food for the entire herd among other products.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T14:33:11-07:00","id":1493431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493430#post1493430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah yes I somehow forgot to conclude that tangent.<br /> <br /> A herd bunker doesn't need to be independent? Getting supplies from outside is easy?<br /> It's entirely possible for vampires to keep their herd in a secure place like an underground bunker or prison and have them fed and supplied by farms and other stuff outside the facility. Today's farming technology is pretty great so vampires will have an easy time using a few easily controlled farmers to provide food for the entire herd among other products.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so you get around it by not having a sealed bunker in the first place. Just keep in mind that means you will be less secure then that guy who seals themselves up and never opens the door (open doors are a security weakness). Not to mention the fact you will be kind of screwed if someone cuts you off from your outside supply source compared to a 'self sufficient' facility.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-20T22:04:04-07:00","id":1493452,"title":"","content":"1-such a bunker would be more likely to be secret in comparison to an all-inclusive bunker. Yes, the crop field above you is more likely to be seen, but crop fields aren't terribly conspicuous things. An entirely self-sustaining underground bunker for a few hundred people would be.... an ordeal. You could probably do a big part of it internally but <br /> 2-who designs an underground city without an emergency exit? Also remember that vampires can do a lot of things mortals can't so they are very likely to take advantage of it. <br /> 3-Who designs an underground bunker without a stockpile that can last you at least two weeks? A vampire with enemies will undoubtedly plan for more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T00:14:13-07:00","id":1493510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493393#post1493393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine what Automation will do to the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our current work circumstances would be alien to the manufacturing pre-industrial society, yet here we are. While your assumptions are perfectly valid as a starting point for a sample scenario, you're just pretending they're a solid prediction instead of puerile assumptions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493393#post1493393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or society will be pushed towards an authoritarian hierarchy or worse, anarcho capitalism, which is essentially fuedalism but with business owners rather than warriors. either of which are excellent for the working class and provide the best possible habbitat for vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever our society, or better, societ<b>ies</b> will be pushed towards is besides the point.<br /> <br /> There would still be no reason to think all vampires would reach the same conclusion and build the same answer to the new challenges. <b>That</b> is beyond stupid no matter how I look at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493393#post1493393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's no need for a masquerade, what do you think vampires would do? If the mortals could truly do nothing against their oppressors, would it make sense to enforce the masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing the Masquerade, I think the proposed exercise is valid. Indeed, I think the Masquerade is the least believable aspect of the traditional setting.<br /> <br /> At most I think your current position on why mortals would be powerless and all vampires would work out together this evil empire without breaking it from within before really achieving it is too hard to believe. It is simplistic and based on childish reductions of social dynamics. I want to see a better, more refined scenario for this. The proposal itself, I'm all for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493251-mieyerditch-what-if-the-kindred-did-want-to-treat-the-kine-like-cattle?p=1493452#post1493452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1-such a bunker would be more likely to be secret in comparison to an all-inclusive bunker. Yes, the crop field above you is more likely to be seen, but crop fields aren't terribly conspicuous things. An entirely self-sustaining underground bunker for a few hundred people would be.... an ordeal. You could probably do a big part of it internally but<br /> 2-who designs an underground city without an emergency exit? Also remember that vampires can do a lot of things mortals can't so they are very likely to take advantage of it.<br /> 3-Who designs an underground bunker without a stockpile that can last you at least two weeks? A vampire with enemies will undoubtedly plan for more.</div> </div> </div> </div>To go with such a bunker the whole idea of keeping the world in chains and devoid of tech is made pointless.<br /> <br /> You control the world, you keep the world in a Dark Age to avoid dangerous weapons, then you make a technological fortress for you to live in with a technological farm above to feed your humans, so you can live for eternity confined to your fortress instead of ruling openly in the world you conquered, although you actually have to leave your fortress to implement the maintenance of the <i>status quo</i>. You also have to make a diet, since you're restricting yourself to a relatively small population of healthy modern mortals most of the time, while the population at large faces the many problems of malnutrition and lack of healthcare, specially for babies and children (the greatest victims in this regard, as the major problem with life expectancy in the past was the huge mortality rate <i><b>before</b></i>around 20 years).<br /> <br /> For a scenario where the point is for vampires to rule humanity openly, treating mortals like cattle, this &quot;plunge the world in the Dark Ages and go live in a bunker&quot; idea seems pretty shitty. If it happens a century in the future and those bunkers are self-sufficient by author fiat, then we can build something interesting for that, but with modern tech it seems they would had a far better prospect just keeping in secret. The problem is not the bunker <i>per se</i>, but the Dark Ages part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T06:28:22-07:00","id":1494520,"title":"","content":"vampire rulers could potentially be better than a lot of RW rulers. The vampiric aristocracy would have fewer needs than human aristocracy (IE they don't eat, want to ensure everyone's well fed, and they're active for less time in the day so they'll spend less on luxuries) and so apart from blood tithes they would likely be less economically draining than, say, Bolsonaro or Liz Truss or whatever regressive feudalistic crackpot you want a comparison to.<br /> <br /> But yeah, we're talking abuse of power here...<br /> <br /> Somewhat reasonable example of how things could change. Now I'm not a Brazilian* so feel free to correct me when I'm wrong, and I actually had a longer more detailed post but it'd maybe be a bit inappropriate, but anyhow:<br /> Brazil is soon to have a second round of voting in its presidential election. It's between the incumbent and far-right Bolsonaro and the socialist Luca, who is almost certainly going to win the popular vote if I'm reading the first-round right. However, given the election interference seen so far it looks very possible that Bolsonaro will cheat or refuse to step down, and given how many powerful people have a vested interest in keeping Luca out and Bolsonaro in, it's likely that things will be a lot worse than Trump's capitol hill riot. From the English language sources I have, it seems violence is probable.<br /> <br /> Does Bolsonaro need Vampires to stay in power? No. The means of violence are largely on his side. However, it would be a great time for vampires to step up their control. When your choices are fascism or socialism, any Vampire worth his blood will be overwhelmingly in favour of fascism. The reality of undead living relies on inequality and corruption so that vampire can feed easily without getting due process. Socialism or any movement towards the left would reduce the inequality which would in turn undermine that corruption: thus, Bolsonaro strengthens the vampires, vampires should therefore strengthen Bolsonaro. When the repressions begin, they can only continue until any resistance has been hounded out. In a modern world, where people have the internet and outside information and are exposed to alternative ideas, is that likely? No, you'll continue to foster dissent, so you can only get more extreme with your methods. So now we move into fiction: Vampires take over a fascist Brazil. With no international power willing to intervene, we might get an undead state.<br /> <br /> Vampire rulers are optional, but they <i>work</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*I do have a lot of Brazilian students though. So hopefully I'm not too off base</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-07-2022, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}